# Serverless Endpoint: Cosmos Reason 2 (primary scene model) self-hosted with vLLM. GPU required.
# Pattern: https://docs.nebius.com/serverless/tutorials/deploy-model.md
# Model flags: https://github.com/nvidia-cosmos/cosmos-reason2 (vllm>=0.11.0, --max-model-len 8192-16384,
# --reasoning-parser qwen3). 8B needs >= 32 GB GPU memory; validated on Hopper and Blackwell.
ENDPOINT_NAME=clearance-cosmos-reason2
# Gated on Hugging Face (auto-approve): HF_TOKEN required.
VISION_MODEL_ID=nvidia/Cosmos-Reason2-8B
# Tag used in the Nebius tutorial. VERIFY it serves Qwen3-VL based models (needs vllm>=0.11.0).
VLLM_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.18.0-cu130
# H100 80 GB in eu-north1. Confirm with account: GPU quota for gpu-h100-sxm.
ENDPOINT_PLATFORM=gpu-h100-sxm
ENDPOINT_PRESET=1gpu-16vcpu-200gb
# Room for model weights, the vLLM image and the CUDA graph cache. VERIFY the size on first start.
ENDPOINT_DISK=150Gi
ENDPOINT_PORT=8000
ENDPOINT_SHM=16Gi
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=16384
